      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start, but can we make them a bit more... evocative? For the first part, I want to really lean into that sense of \"primitive\" simplicity. Like, emphasize how they were more guided by instinct and the natural world rather than complex logic. Maybe use words that suggest a more spiritual or raw way of living. \n\nThen for the second part, I want it to feel much more intellectual and organized. Focus on the power of the human mind and how we moved past those basic, instinctual ways into a world of logic, reason, and mastery over the environment. Can you rewrite them with that contrast in mind?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
